{"title": "Sectional Mock #80 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A seller earns a profit of 25% after selling 60 kg of rice. He adds some impurities in the rice and sells it at the cost price. Find the weight of impurities in 60 kg of rice.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2325;&#2352; 25% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2309;&#2358;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2358;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["14 kg", "15 kg", "12 kg", "10 kg"], "options_hi": ["14 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "15 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "10 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let cost price of 1 kg of rice = &#8377;100</p><p>Selling price of 60 kg of rice = &#8377;6000</p><p>Cost price of 60 kg of rice = &#8377;6000 *(100/125) = &#8377;4800</p><p>Total weight of rice = 4800/100 = 48 kg</p><p>Hence, the weight of impurities in 60 kg of rice = 60  -  48 = 12 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let cost price of 1 kg of rice = &#8377;100</p><p>Selling price of 60 kg of rice = &#8377;6000</p><p>Cost price of 60 kg of rice = &#8377;6000 *(100/125) = &#8377;4800</p><p>Total weight of rice = 4800/100 = 48 kg</p><p>Hence, the weight of impurities in 60 kg of rice = 60  -  48 = 12 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the average of the prime numbers lying between 69 and 92.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>69 &#2324;&#2352; 92 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["79", "82", "80", "81"], "options_hi": ["79", "82", "80", "81"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Prime numbers lying between 69 and 92 = 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Average = (71 + 73 + 79 + 83 + 89)/5 = 395/5 = 79</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Prime numbers lying between 69 and 92 = 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Average = (71 + 73 + 79 + 83 + 89)/5 = 395/5 = 79</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the total surface area of a pyramid which is based on a rectangle of length 70 cm and breadth 10 cm, and height 12 cm?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; 70 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1980 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2720 cm<sup>2</sup>", "3280 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2980 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["1980 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "2720 &#8203;&#8203;&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "3280 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "2980 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>[In this pyramid, two slant heights, one from the base side and the other from the length side]</p><p>Slant height (Base) = &radic;[12<sup>2</sup> + (10/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[144 + 25] = 13 cm</p><p>Slant height (Length) = &radic;[1<sup>2</sup> + (35/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[144 + 9] = 37 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area = 2 * 1/2 * base * slant height + 2 * 1/2 * length * slant height</p><p>= 10 * 37 + 70 * 10</p><p>= 1280cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total surface area of pyramid = Lateral surface area + Base area</p><p>= 1280+ 70 * 10</p><p>= 1980cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[In this pyramid, two slant heights, one from the base side and the other from the length side]</p><p>Slant height (Base) = &radic;[12<sup>2</sup> + (10/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[144 + 25] = 13 cm</p><p>Slant height (Length) = &radic;[1<sup>2</sup> + (35/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[144 + 9] = 37 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area = 2 * 1/2 * base * slant height + 2 * 1/2 * length * slant height</p><p>= 10 * 37 + 70 * 10</p><p>= 1280cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total surface area of pyramid = Lateral surface area + Base area</p><p>= 1280+ 70 * 10</p><p>= 1980cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A container contains 14.4 kg mixture of rice flour and wheat flour in the ratio of 1: 1. If 4.8 kg of mixture is replaced by wheat flour followed by 2.4 kg of mixture again replaced by wheat flour, then what will be the ratio of wheat flour to rice flour in the final mixture?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1: 1 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; 14.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 4.8 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2369;&#2344;&#2307; 2.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["4: 9", "13: 5", "5: 11", "11: 4"], "options_hi": ["4: 9", "13: 5", "5: 11", "11: 4"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Initially, Quantity of rice flour = 14.4 * 1/2 = 7.2 kg and Quantity of wheat flour 14.4 * 1/2 = 7.2 kg</p><p>After 1st operation,</p><p>Quantity of rice flour = 7.2  -  2.4 = 4.8 kg and Quantity of wheat flour = 7.2  -  2.4 + 4.8 = 9.6 kg</p><p>After 2nd operation,</p><p>Quantity of rice flour = 4.8  -  2.4 * 1/3 = 4.0 kg and Quantity of wheat flour 9.6  -  2.4 * 2/3 + 2.4 = 10.4 kg</p><p>So, required ratio = 104: 40 = 13: 5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Initially, Quantity of rice flour = 14.4 * 1/2 = 7.2 kg and Quantity of wheat flour 14.4 * 1/2 = 7.2 kg</p><p>After 1st operation,</p><p>Quantity of rice flour = 7.2  -  2.4 = 4.8 kg and Quantity of wheat flour = 7.2  -  2.4 + 4.8 = 9.6 kg</p><p>After 2nd operation,</p><p>Quantity of rice flour = 4.8  -  2.4 * 1/3 = 4.0 kg and Quantity of wheat flour 9.6  -  2.4 * 2/3 + 2.4 = 10.4 kg</p><p>So, required ratio = 104: 40 = 13: 5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If X =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2 sin &theta;", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2 sin &theta;", "options_en": ["x/(1 + x)", "x", "1/x", "(1 + x)/x"], "options_hi": ["x/(1 + x)", "x", "1/x", "(1 + x)/x"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=124 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image101.png\"></p><p><img width=236 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image102.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image103.png\"></p><p><img width=183 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image104.png\"></p><p><img width=196 height=51 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image105.png\"></p><p><img width=161 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image106.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image107.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image108.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image109.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=124 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image101.png\"></p><p><img width=236 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image102.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image103.png\"></p><p><img width=183 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image104.png\"></p><p><img width=196 height=51 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image105.png\"></p><p><img width=161 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image106.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image107.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image108.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22215/image109.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>The total surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of a cuboid whose volume is 4374 cm<sup>3</sup> and ratio of length: breadth: height is 3:1:2 is</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; 4374 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; : &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312;: &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3: 1: 2 &#2361;&#2376;</p>", "options_en": ["1728", "1782", "891", "864"], "options_hi": ["1728", "1782", "891", "864"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the breadth be l, then length = 3l and height = 2l. </p> <p>Then volume of a cuboid is given by L x B x H = 6l<sup>3</sup></p> <p>Given, 6l<sup>3</sup> = 4374</p> <p>=&gt; l<sup>3</sup>= 729</p> <p>=&gt; l = 9</p> <p>Hence, length = 3l = 27, breadth = l = 9 and height = 2l = 18</p> <p>Now, total surface area of a cuboid is given by 2(LB + BH + HL)</p> <p>= 2 x (27x9 + 9x18 + 18x27)</p> <p>= 1782 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the breadth be l, then length = 3l and height = 2l. </p> <p>Then volume of a cuboid is given by L x B x H = 6l<sup>3</sup></p> <p>Given, 6l<sup>3</sup> = 4374</p> <p>=&gt; l<sup>3</sup>= 729</p> <p>=&gt; l = 9</p> <p>Hence, length = 3l = 27, breadth = l = 9 and height = 2l = 18</p> <p>Now, total surface area of a cuboid is given by 2(LB + BH + HL)</p> <p>= 2 x (27x9 + 9x18 + 18x27)</p> <p>= 1782 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The compound ratio of 6: 13 and 10:14 is X: 26. Find X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>6: 13 &#2324;&#2352; 10:14 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; X: 26 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8", "60/7", "9", "52/7"], "options_hi": ["8", "60/7", "9", "52/7"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(6/13) * (10/14) = X/26</p><p>X = 60/7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(6/13) * (10/14) = X/26</p><p>X = 60/7</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ramesh took a loan of &#8377;41600 from a bank and paid it in two equal installments of &#8377;23200 each at a certain rate of simple interest. What is the rate of interest?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2350;&#2375;&#2358; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; 41600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2315;&#2339; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 23200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["10%", "8%", "4%", "12%"], "options_hi": ["10%", "8%", "4%", "12%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the rate of interest = r%</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>41600(1 + r*2/100) = 23200(1 + r*1/100) + 23200</p><p>416(100 + 2r) = 232(200 + r)</p><p>600r = 4800</p><p>r = 8%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the rate of interest = r%</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>41600(1 + r*2/100) = 23200(1 + r*1/100) + 23200</p><p>416(100 + 2r) = 232(200 + r)</p><p>600r = 4800</p><p>r = 8%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The given pie-chart shows the percentage distribution of runs scored by a batsman in a test innings. Study the chart and answer the question that follows.</p><p><img width=253 height=164 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/erpypimg-40411-28-006.png\" ></p><p>If the batsman has scored a total of 440 runs, how many runs did he score by hitting fours?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312;-&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2348;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2352;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=253 height=164 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/erpypimg-40411-28-006.png\" ></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2348;&#2366;&#2332; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 440 &#2352;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2330;&#2380;&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319;?", "options_en": ["88", "172", "224", "132"], "options_hi": ["88", "172", "224", "132"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Runs from fours = (30 / 100)  X  440</p><p>=&gt; Runs from fours = 0.30  X  440 = 132</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Runs from fours = (30 / 100)  X  440</p><p>=&gt; Runs from fours = 0.30  X  440 = 132</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If x = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'><span style='font-size: 19px;'>&radic;", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'><span style='font-size: 19px;'>&radic;", "options_en": ["350", "345", "284", "322"], "options_hi": ["350", "345", "284", "322"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=227 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20788/image016.png\"></p><p><img width=231 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20788/image017.png\"></p><p>So, <img width=167 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20788/image018.png\"></p><p>=&gt; x + 1/x = 18</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> + 2 = 324</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + x<sup>-2</sup> = 322</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=227 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20788/image016.png\"></p><p><img width=231 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20788/image017.png\"></p><p>So, <img width=167 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20788/image018.png\"></p><p>=&gt; x + 1/x = 18</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> + 2 = 324</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + x<sup>-2</sup> = 322</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given figure, PQ, QS and ST are three tangents to the circle. If QS = 28 cm and ST = 3PQ/4, then find the sum of length of RS and ST.</p><p><img width=167 height=171 id=image2.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image015.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, PQ, QS &#2324;&#2352; ST &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; QS = 28 cm &#2324;&#2352; ST = 3PQ/4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; RS &#2324;&#2352; ST &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"167\" height=\"171\" id=\"image2.png\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image015.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "12 cm", "24 cm"], "options_hi": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "12 cm", "24 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=180 height=184 id=image5.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image016.png\"></p><p>QS = 28 cm and ST = 3PQ/4</p><p>and PQ = QR and RS = ST</p><p>QR + SR = 28</p><p>So, PQ + ST = 28</p><p>PQ + 3PQ/4 = 28</p><p>PQ = 16 cm</p><p>ST = 16*3/4 = 12 cm</p><p>&#8757; RS + ST = 12 + 12 = 24 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=180 height=184 id=image5.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22741/image016.png\"></p><p>QS = 28 cm and ST = 3PQ/4</p><p>and PQ = QR and RS = ST</p><p>QR + SR = 28</p><p>So, PQ + ST = 28</p><p>PQ + 3PQ/4 = 28</p><p>PQ = 16 cm</p><p>ST = 16*3/4 = 12 cm</p><p>&#8757; RS + ST = 12 + 12 = 24 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train of length 90 meters moving with 11 m/s crosses another train of length 'L' meters which is moving in same direction with 32.4 km/hr in 88 seconds. What is the value of 'L'?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>11 m/s &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; 90 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;, &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 32.4 km/hr &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; 'L' &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 88 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 'L' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["76", "86", "92", "108"], "options_hi": ["76", "86", "92", "108"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of one train = 11 m/s</p><p>Speed of another train = 32.4 * 5/18 = 9 m/s</p><p>Since both the trains are moving in same direction. So, relative speed = 11  -  9 = 2 m/s</p><p>Now, time taken by one train to cross the other = (sum of lengths of both the trains)/(relative speed)</p><p>88 = (90 + L)/2</p><p>176 = 90 + L</p><p><b>L = 86</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of one train = 11 m/s</p><p>Speed of another train = 32.4 * 5/18 = 9 m/s</p><p>Since both the trains are moving in same direction. So, relative speed = 11  -  9 = 2 m/s</p><p>Now, time taken by one train to cross the other = (sum of lengths of both the trains)/(relative speed)</p><p>88 = (90 + L)/2</p><p>176 = 90 + L</p><p><b>L = 86</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 7<sup>a</sup> = 11<sup>b</sup> = 77<sup>c</sup>, then find the value of c = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 7<sup>a</sup> = 11<sup>b</sup> = 77<sup>c</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; c &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; = ?</p>", "options_en": ["1/a  -  a/b + 1/c = 0", "1/a  -  1/b  -  1/c = 0", "1/a + 1/b + 1/c = 0", "1/a + 1/b  -  1/c = 0"], "options_hi": ["1/a  -  a/b + 1/c = 0", "1/a  -  1/b  -  1/c = 0", "1/a + 1/b + 1/c = 0", "1/a + 1/b  -  1/c = 0"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>7<sup>a</sup> = 11<sup>b</sup> = 77<sup>c</sup></p><p>Let 7<sup>a</sup> = 11<sup>b</sup> = 77<sup>c</sup> = k</p><p>7 = k<sup>1/a</sup>............(i)</p><p>11 = k<sup>1/b</sup>............(ii)</p><p>77 = k<sup>1/c</sup>...........(iii)</p><p>7 * 11 = 77</p><p>k<sup>1/a</sup> * k<sup>1/b</sup> = k<sup>1/c</sup>............using eq(i), (ii) and (iii)</p><p>k<sup>1/A</sup> <sup>+ 1/B</sup> = k<sup>1/C</sup></p><p>1/a + 1/b = 1/c</p><p>1/a + 1/b  -  1/c = 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>7<sup>a</sup> = 11<sup>b</sup> = 77<sup>c</sup></p><p>Let 7<sup>a</sup> = 11<sup>b</sup> = 77<sup>c</sup> = k</p><p>7 = k<sup>1/a</sup>............(i)</p><p>11 = k<sup>1/b</sup>............(ii)</p><p>77 = k<sup>1/c</sup>...........(iii)</p><p>7 * 11 = 77</p><p>k<sup>1/a</sup> * k<sup>1/b</sup> = k<sup>1/c</sup>............using eq(i), (ii) and (iii)</p><p>k<sup>1/A</sup> <sup>+ 1/B</sup> = k<sup>1/C</sup></p><p>1/a + 1/b = 1/c</p><p>1/a + 1/b  -  1/c = 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ashutosh and Aarav started a business by investing &#8377;10800 and &#8377;14400 respectively. What is the share of Ashutosh if the total profit received by Aarav after one year is &#8377;1780?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2358;&#2369;&#2340;&#2379;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#8377;10800 &#2324;&#2352; &#8377;14400 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#8377;1780 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2358;&#2369;&#2340;&#2379;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2306;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;1450", "&#8377;1648", "&#8377;1335", "&#8377;1260"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;1450", "&#8377;1648", "&#8377;1335", "&#8377;1260"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of share of Ashutosh and Aarav = 10800:14400 = 3:4</p><p>Share of Aarav = 1780 * 3/4 = &#8377;1335</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of share of Ashutosh and Aarav = 10800:14400 = 3:4</p><p>Share of Aarav = 1780 * 3/4 = &#8377;1335</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If cosec A =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a + b", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cosec A = <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a + b", "options_en": ["(a + b)<sup>2</sup>/(a - b)", "(a + b)<sup>2</sup>/(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)", "(a - b)<sup>2</sup>/(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)", "(a - b)<sup>2</sup>/(a + b)"], "options_hi": ["(a + b)<sup>2</sup>/(a - b)", "(a + b)<sup>2</sup>/(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)", "(a - b)<sup>2</sup>/(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)", "(a - b)<sup>2</sup>/(a + b)"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=101 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=127 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=93 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=133 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=167 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=139 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image042.png\"></p><p><img width=112 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image043.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image044.png\"></p><p><img width=168 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image045.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image046.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=101 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=123 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=127 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=93 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=133 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=167 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=139 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image042.png\"></p><p><img width=112 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image043.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image044.png\"></p><p><img width=168 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image045.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16025/image046.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Tarun is twice as good as Tripti in doing a work. Together, they can complete the work in 16 days. In how many days can Tripti alone complete the same work? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2309;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2357;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 16 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["24", "48", "25", "50"], "options_hi": ["24", "48", "25", "50"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Efficiency of Tarun and Tripti = 2:1</p><p>Total work = (2 + 1)*16 = 48 units</p><p>Time taken by Tripti alone = 48/1 = 48 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Efficiency of Tarun and Tripti = 2:1</p><p>Total work = (2 + 1)*16 = 48 units</p><p>Time taken by Tripti alone = 48/1 = 48 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the compound interest received after 2.5 years at 16% rate of compound interest compounded annually on &#8377;40000.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>'40000' &#2346;&#2352; 16% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 2.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;10408.56", "&#8377;12590.84", "&#8377;18129.92", "&#8377;21346.05"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;10408.56", "&#8377;12590.84", "&#8377;18129.92", "&#8377;21346.05"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Amount received after 2 years = 40000(1+16/100)<sup>2</sup> = 53824</p><p>Amount received after 2.5 years = = 53824 + 53824*16*6/(100*12) = &#8377;58129.92 </p><p>Compound interest received after 2.5 years = 58129.92  -  40000 = &#8377;18129.92</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount received after 2 years = 40000(1+16/100)<sup>2</sup> = 53824</p><p>Amount received after 2.5 years = = 53824 + 53824*16*6/(100*12) = &#8377;58129.92 </p><p>Compound interest received after 2.5 years = 58129.92  -  40000 = &#8377;18129.92</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A invests &#8377;80000 for 12 months. B invests &#8377;60000 for the first 6 months and then increases it to &#8377;80000 for the next 6 months. C invests &#8377;70000 for 9 months. If total profit is &#8377;243000, what is B's share (in Rs.)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A 12 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;80000 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; B &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;60000 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#8377;80000 &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; C 9 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;70000 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#8377;243000 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["81000", "84000", "87000", "90000"], "options_hi": ["81000", "84000", "87000", "90000"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of the investment of A, B and C =</p><p>80000 X 12 : (60000 X 6 + 80000 X 6) : 70000 X 9</p><p>= 96: 84 : 63</p><p>Total profit = &#8377;243000</p><p>B's Share = &#8377;243000 * 84/243 = &#8377;84000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of the investment of A, B and C =</p><p>80000 X 12 : (60000 X 6 + 80000 X 6) : 70000 X 9</p><p>= 96: 84 : 63</p><p>Total profit = &#8377;243000</p><p>B's Share = &#8377;243000 * 84/243 = &#8377;84000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The value of 42.6 out of 1000 in decimal fraction is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1000 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 42.6 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["0.0426", "0.426", "0.00426", "4.26"], "options_hi": ["0.0426", "0.426", "0.00426", "4.26"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the number of common tangents, if r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>1</sub> C<sub>2</sub>. (With usual notations, r<sub>1</sub> &amp; r<sub>2</sub> and C<sub>1</sub> &amp; C<sub>2</sub> are the radii and centres of the two circles.)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; r<sub>1</sub> + r<sub>2</sub> = C<sub>1</sub> C<sub>2 </sub>(&#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2325;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; r<sub>1</sub> &#2324;&#2352; r<sub>2 </sub> &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; C<sub>1</sub> &#2324;&#2352; C<sub>2</sub> &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "0", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "0", "3", "4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>If <img width=13 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image017.png\">+ <img width=15 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image021.png\"> = <img width=35 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image022.png\">, then there are 3 common tangents (2 direct and 1 transverse) .</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If <img width=13 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image017.png\">+ <img width=15 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image021.png\"> = <img width=35 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image022.png\">, then there are 3 common tangents (2 direct and 1 transverse) .</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The breadth of a cuboid is b cm. The length of the cuboid is three times its breadth and the height of the cuboid is the average of its length and breadth. Find the total surface area (in sq. cm) of cuboid.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; b cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (sq. cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["12b<sup>2</sup>", "22b<sup>2</sup>", "16b<sup>2</sup>", "28b<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["12b<sup>2</sup>", "22b<sup>2</sup>", "16b<sup>2</sup>", "28b<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Breadth = b cm</p><p>length = 3b cm</p><p>Height = 2b cm</p><p>Total surface area = 2 * (lb+bh +hl) = 2 * (3b<sup>2</sup> + 2b<sup>2</sup> + 6b<sup>2</sup>) = 22b<sup>2</sup> cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Breadth = b cm</p><p>length = 3b cm</p><p>Height = 2b cm</p><p>Total surface area = 2 * (lb+bh +hl) = 2 * (3b<sup>2</sup> + 2b<sup>2</sup> + 6b<sup>2</sup>) = 22b<sup>2</sup> cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A retailer cheats his wholesaler and customer both. He purchases (X + 5) % more from the wholesaler and sells (X  -  5) % less while selling to his customer. Find the value of X, if the profit percentage by selling the goods at cost price is 33(1/3)%</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2341;&#2379;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2331;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2341;&#2379;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; (X + 5)% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (X - 5)% &#2325;&#2350; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 33(1/3)% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["15", "10", "20", "25"], "options_hi": ["15", "10", "20", "25"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>From the statements, he purchases (105 + X) g instead of 100g and he sells (105  -  X) g instead of 100 and (105- X) &lt; 100.</p><p>Therefore, in the whole transaction he gains = (105 + X  -  100) + (100  -  105 + X)</p><p>= 5 + X + X  -  5 = 2X gm</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>(2X) * 100/ (105  -  X) = 100/3</p><p>6X = 105  -  X</p><p>7X = 105</p><p>X = 15.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From the statements, he purchases (105 + X) g instead of 100g and he sells (105  -  X) g instead of 100 and (105- X) &lt; 100.</p><p>Therefore, in the whole transaction he gains = (105 + X  -  100) + (100  -  105 + X)</p><p>= 5 + X + X  -  5 = 2X gm</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>(2X) * 100/ (105  -  X) = 100/3</p><p>6X = 105  -  X</p><p>7X = 105</p><p>X = 15.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of milk and water in a 91l mixture is 4: 3. Some quantity of milk is removed from the mixture, and the ratio of milk to water becomes 12: 13. How much milk is removed? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>911 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4: 3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 12: 13 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16l", "18l", "24l", "22l"], "options_hi": ["16l", "18l", "24l", "22l"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The milk in a mixture = 91*4/7 = 52l</p><p>The water in a mixture = 91  -  52 = 39 l</p><p>Let the milk removed from the mixture be 'x'.</p><p>A/Q</p><p>(52  -  x)/ 39 = 12/13 </p><p>52* 13  -  13x = 39* 12</p><p>676  -  13x = 468</p><p>13x = 676  -  468</p><p>x = 208/13 = 16l</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The milk in a mixture = 91*4/7 = 52l</p><p>The water in a mixture = 91  -  52 = 39 l</p><p>Let the milk removed from the mixture be 'x'.</p><p>A/Q</p><p>(52  -  x)/ 39 = 12/13 </p><p>52* 13  -  13x = 39* 12</p><p>676  -  13x = 468</p><p>13x = 676  -  468</p><p>x = 208/13 = 16l</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If <img width=145 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image011.png\">, <img width=132 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image012.png\">, and <img width=145 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image013.png\">, then what is the value of (P  X  Q &div; R)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; <img width=145 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image011.png\">, <img width=132 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image012.png\">, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; <img width=145 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image013.png\">, &#2340;&#2379; (P X Q &div; R) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["(5x  -  3y)", "(3x  -  2y)", "(x + 3y)", "1"], "options_hi": ["(5x  -  3y)", "(3x  -  2y)", "(x + 3y)", "1"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=403 height=141 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image014.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=403 height=141 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16669/image014.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat takes 4.5 hours to travel 90 km in upstream. If the speed of boat in still water is 24 km/h, then find the speed of stream. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 90 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 4.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 24 km/h &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["5 km/h", "3.6 km/h", "6 km/h", "4 km/h"], "options_hi": ["5 km/h", "3.6 km/h", "6 km/h", "4 km/h"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the speed of stream = 'u' km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in still water = 24 km/h</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>90/(24  -  u) = 4.5</p><p>24  -  u = 20</p><p>u = 4 km/h</p><p>Hence, the speed of stream = 4 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the speed of stream = 'u' km/h</p><p>Speed of boat in still water = 24 km/h</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>90/(24  -  u) = 4.5</p><p>24  -  u = 20</p><p>u = 4 km/h</p><p>Hence, the speed of stream = 4 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}]}